# (0.17.53) A PHRASE ON THE PLUCK KEEPS THE CHORD: on JAM, Chords mode, a key plays a triad; recorded into the phrase, it comes back as the same
# three notes at once (before: its root alone). The acid and the bass are one note at a time and stay so.
seed 0
wait 3000
turn SELECT 36 100
expect view 36
expect jamv 0
spin K2 1
wait 50
expect jamm 1
# the chord played live: its notes out on channel 2
midireset
key 13 down
wait 150
key 13 up
wait 50
expect cmmax 3
expect cmpcs 0x221
tap REC
expect phrase 1
key 13 down
wait 100
expect phrase 2
wait 300
key 13 up
wait 100
expect phnotes 1
expect phchords 1
tap REC
waitfor phrase 3 5000
expect ph_v 4
# played back (the pluck's own line is off meanwhile): the same three notes at once, nothing else
midireset
wait 4000
expect cmmax 3
expect cmpcs 0x221
shot phrasechord.png
